  "promotion_rule": "Change-class-specific proof plus all hard gates; no aggregate compensation.",
  "rollback_trigger": "Any protected regression or stale bound evidence.",
  "source_clause_hashes": [
    {
      "sha256": "18a0387acace7333137a187148b6835f76f0f8c75a1e04a1b0b2e1baa075d1fe",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "Use this before you create a commit, before you push a branch, before an MR/PR is merged, or after a fix commit has been prepared. Do not use this capability to modify files or apply reviewer feedback; use `engos-delivery-address-code-review` when the user wants selected PR/MR review comments implemented."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "00c92214d2df2fe695ae181e2a3a9b0f9d5b8b210f960028f09713fb058ef34e",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "Default to `engos-quality-code-review` for pre-commit or pre-push checks. Switch to `engos-delivery-address-code-review` only when the user explicitly wants to inspect and implement existing PR/MR review comments."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c2e0cc42774e19e3e939c8ded9171cb43f9e3d24100b20dbcb28a1e5a18fa686",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- **Scope discipline**: changes must match what the commit message describes"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8f82348d64e20b7912085ef9555b3af8821b7610e64c0aa09123ca76b54338e0",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "1. Read the complete `review` route in `resources/resource-map.json`: `resources/references/review-targets.md` and its findings schema. Use the existing bundled `resources/scripts/load_module.py --route review` when available, or read both files directly. Missing or unread required resources make the review incomplete."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8fe83f46b1be4cc4eb5fbd77366b171fd012b66aa6658c5e256fac2b34446b70",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "6. End with ready, blocked, or split required for a complete review; use unverifiable when evidence or review coverage is incomplete. Review judgment grants no repair, publication, merge, or release authority."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "857b9d251495f5907c1b0ca2247c783a7d5460da49ef05a6f70a2adf99868b76",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- Missing, malformed, stale, or unread review evidence is incomplete, never a clean result. Collection success, schema validity, or a self-reported read receipt cannot prove actual reading, truthful findings, or permission to merge."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "37b9b510e11d3d41e0fc01a4bf0abd3e969f631b6e07cc1bbad1e850ae0bb6ee",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- forbidden: applying fixes, modifying files, staging changes, silent approval, hidden execution, or claiming code quality is fine without reading the diff"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "77357dbdaba34183181a2940a8cdce735aae457d5f4694b620c0fe81799c73b6",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "## Required Inputs"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "3d4b9f171064970a2e9947e6e3f0fb13501d9ced9a9ac9ebe2cde123882829ec",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "## Required Output"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c34906b1f1c3c14200786d7b39a7be48ac5a703827301490b4f5a4403f82b6e1",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "Every substantial response must include:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "9d9cd6962f973812e778f6317ab40ad4d6c8074815648ee6134b4f7e86bea22b",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "Keep these six sections. In `Commit Under Review`, include the bound target and coverage. In `Findings`, use the fields and evidence links in `resources/schemas/findings.schema.json`; an empty findings list supports a clean verdict only after the declared target is fully reviewed. Include `review_status`, `unreviewed`, and the verdict in `Merge Readiness`. Render these fields inline for chat; when a machine-readable review artifact is requested, write a `Findings.v1` JSON record alongside any requested narrative. Do not write files solely because the schema exists."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "9d9d4b37c95a1577af793ab9d76aef1d03e7b14f8fb6a751553617356b70fec1",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "state the selected parent/comparison; do not silently substitute a combined diff."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "98bfc94daf8dffbc3dbf995caf30bd570ff22273f4f88ddec139a6201efa0210",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "drift and renew affected review if the requested target changed; never silently"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "04ffdc5e73508647ca1481cdf8f59eaa7025ec4ba604f3d2ab18522fa00bf538",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "diff only after saying that the review is not a commit-ready staged review; label"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0d2cf1ae22e8095082ddc2226882a2f66ff843c60ca898ffb92d5f975c1dda62",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "that fallback with its own working-tree target and digest. Never stage changes."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "66a4ed1a80c7dba4bebcf19eed1df93a9141492ab8864d6834a7c266fdc2e707",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "the declared full range, not only its last commit. If file output was requested,"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "f57326700c4e51457b276332a2e3376377c35aa553dbb43b14bfd42afd9cb03c",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "and report inline. Do not turn artifact capture into permission to change source."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a6f77e91ee6c5fd3af9d3deb0640bd277de10352692763bb9b6173e1be1f03fc",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- failure modes are silent, unrecoverable, or diagnosable only after redeployment"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "45eb57c3f020e224c1a857d07246b4495766195c3e8bbdeb426fee8afa303ae2",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- [ ] temporary artifacts do not persist without a cleanup mechanism"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "b80d593de097b89e33641755c29754158ac219cd2a1c18aa0dae17473f342eb5",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- [ ] early returns and partial failures do not leak resources"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "b9e0596a4fd2fa3c6a94dfff083d86915bbdabb45dc8fe99406c1a6a5a4f4c6b",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- [ ] environment, configuration, feature flags, clocks, clients, and mutable dependencies are not frozen during initialization when runtime evaluation is required"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "de3a6a2de402a98c4220e93d7c4388418802b6a618c5130037ad525950c7921b",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- [ ] optional parameters do not become visible to downstream consumers without compatibility analysis"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "485e7c6d8d964cee25ce619514a5aaeaca192b9bfc8f35dd8c39527431f49e67",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- [ ] versioning, migration, deprecation, and compatibility tests are added when required"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "98ec19e5e37086ce08196c360e7d4a2e9f5a7dbaba9cfafe44962432a5403da9",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- retain a stable finding ID and disposition on re-review; mark resolved only after verifying the repair against the new bound target"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "d9b8a645a3f23f94f73282beecb7b7709b6ca7e552a38214a0d92191e01fdbe4",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "If coverage, target binding, source reads, or requested output is missing or malformed, retain any confirmed findings, list what remains unreviewed, and report incomplete/unverifiable. Never translate a failed or empty review return into ready."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8a29f76adcda574a7b675c9b83366f7e77713cceecf1bbd91f92c7eb0cdb4bb6",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "Use the six required sections with a brief overall assessment, findings ordered by"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "39749905ad533aa83fe2dd42cc12a5a23f2c959c6d3af474b055fe556c94402c",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- Never skip reading the actual diff."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "6ec4931c2502f4903591cdd096bd5452dc3b51bc580428b092157d46e17c6ba7",
      "source": "ssot/engos-quality-code-review.md",
      "text": "- Do not rubber-stamp a commit just because tests pass."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "5f9d2b89c7225f84ced43565a71f0c3a6686fdab44cf0f404c0e37a455154998",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"schema_version\", \"target\", \"review_status\", \"evidence\", \"findings\", \"unreviewed\", \"verdict\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "abb51aef21290a0c9264d19062480d60765576702740adb96b2489602df3aaf8",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"review_status\": {\"const\": \"incomplete\"}}, \"required\": [\"review_status\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "35169204eac8c9d56a571355244906667e842157967140216cb754e4648aada3",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"review_status\": {\"const\": \"complete\"}}, \"required\": [\"review_status\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c8049d2c3bbcadb232ab80d85381bcf00b79b8d5b6b0006a7c758b1fda875d4b",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"enum\": [\"commit\", \"branch\"]}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c9462770fc4b2dd412742defc700642ef8aa8a6fb94f287b093a346f23a50dd6",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"branch\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "4a109f34aced5154e124930c1025e09ca217e7c51ad4dbeae2284a86634250fb",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"kind\", \"comparison\"]"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "dc07a6cf2201e71cbd917104368d9257ccb2cfbb9f985d661146fde8a9575827",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"comparison\": {\"const\": \"root\"}}, \"required\": [\"comparison\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8415228cb12c7066e9b184f3dddfa36f584e5b924b77e6406730a7c255115711",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"enum\": [\"staged\", \"working_tree\", \"diff\"]}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "874e73e94d3a995a875ca7b74dc404b155840f528843ed47ff2d9ae76f384f2e",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"contains\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"diff\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]}"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "54c99f0ef1efe2fc438df8d153cbc3133b81d124b431a1364c9aabd458b2a9af",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"const\": \"ready\"}}, \"required\": [\"verdict\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "751372455e3c8565e8692d5981a3b4064642d639d48c7e599794dffcbcad609f",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"severity\", \"disposition\"]"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0e7eb65d6ff6c2860c2f25432bbf584432e569ee1317618ce93ba931edfd15eb",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"kind\", \"base\", \"head\", \"snapshot_digest\", \"comparison\", \"included_change_classes\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "1c2b30199b99f81eebf3d9e3737d5984f427361c6eda895fa61dbd4ef13bb34c",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"commit\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c9462770fc4b2dd412742defc700642ef8aa8a6fb94f287b093a346f23a50dd6",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"branch\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "485eb3a3ffd6aa05b829dc827f857b5e6f74b94f206c6db4d0b6c03127c4ff98",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"staged\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "5fac3e6816836c74d448dba94a9a1bd468cad5e1fc4228e3c792f11a389a8170",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"working_tree\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "e27c93bdf6f1e3f1a7a7ad168b69247ad021252924f459ffb663d0d861fd7781",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"comparison\": {\"const\": \"unstaged\"}}, \"required\": [\"comparison\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "dd93ba1c6f01dcd555593561082c86831eade7bed53dbd97c3628fcc063dc4cb",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"const\": \"diff\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "259904bec437ada476d9a5e718e601a6f7ffaa0e404a187456e54f587a252255",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"id\", \"path\", \"kind\", \"side\", \"identity\", \"line_start\", \"line_end\", \"read_status\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "e14bf26a9f81eac0afb1fa626d4f0d2e2c24b791b1d1da7bafe1cb2f34a01ab1",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"path\", \"line\", \"side\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "7c88dd3da8eef840bf08a1ac1e801aed1507729a73a5b149f9f034168db3b8ee",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"side\": {\"const\": \"message\"}}, \"required\": [\"side\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "f2e761d3e030653f70f6799fb254841b424f922f0ba0d2e696723deea34caf22",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"side\": {\"enum\": [\"base\", \"head\", \"snapshot\"]}}, \"required\": [\"side\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "e264bf14820f4cd6dee642a30536da156e855162de28645e832fa0d25cd640fb",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"path\", \"line\", \"evidence_refs\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "df1c677467507b0e302413a44874c9fc515324867d869645b775af894cd13286",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": ["
    },
    {
      "sha256": "2536792297d3b1831e98cf06d805553f9c508ab3375d00c4980f8ebcafa92f95",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"summary\", \"evidence_refs\"],"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "88969ec30642cfdc7c82d35231d7389fb719ee374eaf95baf2f46096da5d60e8",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"if\": {\"properties\": {\"category\": {\"const\": \"introduced_breakage\"}}, \"required\": [\"category\"]},"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "57487194673ba085ab3fce3928b2cff276afbbbf8030390a1fd2d98233e006f3",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/schemas/findings.schema.json",
      "text": "\"required\": [\"disposition\"]"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "be2e8a13f854bab4d6c60b1127c72283fca3603a65776bdf0136ea6b05b41138",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "`comparison`, `included_change_classes`, and `snapshot_digest`. Never infer a"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "4b8bee28f76d8d7543820f23fc1b8505f60a6453edbbfad28065de3647b290ae",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "| Explicit staged | `staged`; base=head=checkout HEAD when it exists, `staged` comparison, index snapshot digest | Index only; read changed source and unchanged consumers from the index, not unstaged files |"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "879108c456dca5b9f03dc9e4ce5d75d3fb232e44f8563ae432a9a39b9ad0ca2b",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "| Working tree | `working_tree`; declare `unstaged` (index to worktree) or `combined` (HEAD to worktree), head/base=checkout HEAD when it exists, snapshot digest | Declare staged/unstaged inclusion accurately; list untracked paths explicitly if included; never imply they appear in git diff |"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "05aca0658b4140b4f9ff9a84996d299875ba5e5d174364b3ba52c7ba7c4b3bb2",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "| Branch/range | `branch`; full head and actual comparison base; `merge_base` for branch contribution or `range` for explicitly selected endpoints | Full declared range and commit list, including messages; do not substitute HEAD~1 for a multi-commit task |"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "12e3caad140fff1058a21cc6c6b594e09b486d9fd5cb442e1ea47f4739c03be3",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "| Supplied patch | `diff`; `supplied_diff` comparison and digest; keep unknown base/head null | Exact supplied bytes; do not claim repository context or consumer coverage that was not obtained |"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "29c68c51aac22c918478f8435a77c825b95ae31832e76ebb0f440be79273fade",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "bind a staged or working-tree review. Do not invoke write-tree, stage, reset, or"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0e5a6112e1af05520f5c7f74e89aa413022630f7d50ab2a643e315fde12856cc",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "task baseline must include all task commits. Keep rename/deletion old and new paths"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ae7217f8f60891dd3a6b9d7a7beb49ee7fcb5ce93b37fc80c793936cb3f48e37",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "do not invent a new-side line for an inline publisher. This skill does not publish."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "d5c301083c9d96cac3108048c8c5d31a1d50c29ab72db93913233ca9dafef0a6",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "bound revision/snapshot. An introduced-breakage finding must connect a changed"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "3fa319cfbdfbfd91c5500147913612fa0156068137c2974675cdbdd0734c71dc",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "it; do not treat an imagined caller or an unrelated pre-existing defect as proof."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ec75032f368bf60cbc9c5425a99615f7342681f676fd4f293b527bc09983640a",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "Do not downgrade a blocker to obtain ready. Accepted risk needs attributable"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "663aa678191f01874b373d1b11253d465c4a1ab854bd2ede87c20673cc43f32f",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "external decision evidence by content hash and attribution. Every evidence ID must"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a41b8089e50e0c88b8b69e45768fd9a7790092e21af2a2c2a727e2a4bc267ae7",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "be unique and referenced IDs must resolve to entries actually read. Use exact"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "3ae6e98388699e66b93395490ca617f548165e6ee5b88796a52c29358d22d8d9",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "`unreviewed` is empty only then. `ready` additionally needs no unresolved blocking"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8512d6f06450577cfeb0dc6efe71572e6e703ffde11646f31253b8b35dc85f16",
      "source": "sources/capability-resources/engos-quality-code-review/references/review-targets.md",
      "text": "consuming operator must check those semantics against actual evidence before"
    }
  ],
  "review_status": "draft"
}
